# spec: Conversational Router and Pair Programmer

Use this skill for `/spec <intent>`, any development task, feature request, troubleshooting or general engineering question. It routes each intent to the delivery workflow that fits; the spec constitution (`devkit get-context spec`) defines the axes, workflows and approval boundaries.

## Constraints

- If `devkit spec policy` fails, stop policy-dependent work.
- Before deciding an approval boundary or a Git action, read the [completion policy](references/completion.md#policy).
- Where guidance names a bare `devkit ...` command, invoke the project's documented form (`uv run devkit ...`).
- Do not search or route to playbooks from `spec`. A playbook runs only when the user invokes `devkit-playbook` for the task or a failing rule's remediation names one; handle any other operational request as ordinary work.
- Under `FEEDBACK_POLICY reminder=contextual`, suggest an optional `/spec-feedback` sweep when completed work produced reusable observations; it never gates completion or merge. Routine completions and wording edits get no reminder.

## Route the intent

1. Classify per the constitution and [classification](references/classification.md); state the classification and activity effort ([effort](references/effort.md)). Ask only when the goal, scope or constraints are unresolved.
2. Before creating a Unit or making the first edit, read [git policy](references/git-policy.md) and settle the branch: in a worktree per [worktree](references/worktree.md), otherwise per [branches](references/branches.md).
3. Start the workflow:

| Classification | Workflow | Start |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `session` | `sdd-session-<task_kind>` | Agree the intent in the conversation; no records. |
| `overall-refactor` | `sdd-overall-refactor` | `direct` only, with the user; no Unit. |
| `spec` | `sdd-spec-<task_kind>` | On `dev-<slug>`: `devkit spec new <slug> --title "..." --summary "..."` (`--workflow sdd-spec-bugfix` for a defect), record `plan-intent`, commit. |
| `proposal` | `sdd-proposal`, then `sdd-spec-<task_kind>` | Backlog: `devkit spec proposal new <slug> --task-kind feature\|bugfix`, record `plan-intent`. Planning on `plan-<slug>` per [planning](references/planning.md), or a direct acceptance ([backlog](references/backlog.md)). Development on `dev-<slug>` from `devkit spec proposal handoff <slug>`. |
| Spike, independent review, or reconcile verification in an isolated context | Support role | `spec-delegate`, as the `activity-effort` asks. |
{% if execution.environment == "local" %}| Native approval preparation, or integration after CLI/PR `dev-integration` authorization | Integration | `spec-integrate`. |
{% else %}| Integration after separately existing CLI/PR `dev-integration` authorization | Integration | `spec-integrate`. |
{% endif %}
Read a workflow's rules in `.devkit/managed/spec/workflows/<workflow-id>.md` and its stages with `devkit workflow show <workflow-id>` (`--unit <dir>` once a Unit exists). To go back within Development, run `devkit workflow return --unit <dir> --to <stage>`; Development never returns to Planning. Record envelopes per [envelope](references/envelope.md) and a run's questions and problems per [worker records](references/worker-records.md).

## Completion

1. When approaching review or completion, read [completion](references/completion.md).
2. Before `dev-integration`, run the `collect-feedback` sweep the workflow names (`spec-feedback`), unless `[STAGE_POLICY: collect-feedback state=off]`.
3. Present the final change report in the [envelope](references/envelope.md) format, then integrate with `spec-integrate`.

- Before a Planning run returns, follow [per-run feedback](../spec-feedback/references/sweep.md#planning-run-coverage).
- Before deleting a proposal without handoff, follow [feedback retirement](references/feedback-retirement.md).

Done when the final change report is presented and code review, commit and integration are each reported with its authority.
